142	\subsection{Grid Search Landscape and the Optimal Plateau}
143	\label{sec:grid}
144	
145	Table~\ref{tab:grid} presents the extended grid search over $b \in \{0.1, 0.2, 0.3, 0.5, 1.0, 2.0, 5.0\}$ at $\rho=0.4$ on Qwen3-0.6B across 3 seeds. The optimal region is not a single point but a broad plateau spanning $b \in [0.3, 0.5]$: the cross-seed mean at $b=0.3$ (17.649) and $b=0.5$ (17.646) differ by only 0.003 PPL, with a paired $t$-test $p=0.42$ (n.s., $n=3$). This plateau has an asymmetric shape---PPL decreases slowly for $b < 0.3$ (from 17.680 at $b=0.1$) but rises sharply for $b > 0.5$---implying that overshooting $b$ is less costly than undershooting.
