274	\subsection{$n_{\min}$ Sensitivity Ablation}
275	\label{sec:nmin_ablation}
276	
277	Table~\ref{tab:nmin} presents the ESS constraint sensitivity ($\rho=0.4$, Qwen3-0.6B, seed42). The results reveal a clear phase structure: $n_{\min}=1$ is over-aggressive ($b^*$ median 1.73, 12.8\% of batches with $b^*>5$) yet still improves over uniform (PPL 17.668); $n_{\min}=2$ is optimal (PPL 17.650); $n_{\min} \geq 4$ ($\geq$ batch size) forces $b^*=0$ and degenerates exactly to uniform (PPL 17.690). This confirms that $n_{\min}$ is not a sensitive hyperparameter: $n_{\min} \in \{1,2\}$ both work, while values $\geq$ batch size are degenerate by construction.
