296	\subsection{Detector Quality Ablation}
297	\label{sec:detector}
298	
299	Table~\ref{tab:detector} compares the lightweight TF-IDF+LR detector (AUC=0.939) against ModernBERT-150M (AUC=0.986). ModernBERT improves adaptive PPL by an additional 0.012 (from 17.650 to 17.638), a 30\% increase in reweighting value. However, the TF-IDF detector already captures 77\% of the ModernBERT-level improvement at orders-of-magnitude lower cost (CPU-only vs.\ GPU fine-tuning of a 150M transformer). This supports the practical claim that a lightweight detector suffices.
300	
301	The $b^*$ distribution adapts to detector quality: ModernBERT's more bimodal $q$-scores (mid-range ratio 0.28 vs.\ 0.46 for TF-IDF) lead to lower $b^*$ (median 0.45 vs.\ 0.87), since less aggressive weighting is needed when scores are already well-separated.
