351	\subsection{Domain-Skewed Contamination}
352	\label{sec:domain_skew}
353	
354	Real web corpora exhibit non-uniform contamination across domains. Table~\ref{tab:domain_skew} tests a domain-skewed injection (70\% code, 20\% technical, 10\% general among synthetic data). Adaptive $b^*$ improves by 0.05 PPL (0.28\% relative), matching uniform-injection performance. Per-batch $b^*$ varies by domain: code-heavy batches receive median $b^*=1.35$ (stronger downweighting) while general-domain batches receive 0.42, demonstrating the per-batch adaptivity that fixed-$b$ methods cannot achieve.
